    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91580.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "That's British Prime Minister Tony Blair talking about his announcement today that Britain will withdraw around 1,600 troops from Iraq in the coming months. He's got right now, Great Britain has a 7,100 strong contingent there by late summer. They hope to have it down to around 5,000. We're going to talk about the implications of that. today on the program. Also, I return today from the National Religious Broadcasters Convention in Orlando. Certainly a great time to see other broadcasters from all over the country, really all over the world. Time of encouragement and also time of education on the threats to the freedoms of religious broadcasters and Christians in general. We'll talk about that a little bit later. We'll also talk about the state of New Jersey, which has begun civil unions, ceremonies, legal civil unions for homosexual couples now in that state. And we continue to cover the implications of Texas Governor's Rick Perry's mandate that girls entering the sixth grade be required to receive the vaccine against a sexually transmitted disease. We're going to talk with a doctor about that. But first of all, let's just hear one more comment from British Prime Minister Tony Blair, addressing the House of Commons. He says the British troops will take on more of a support role for the Iraqi forces.",
