    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "No ma'am. I don't. I think anybody who's visited Iraq and I've not been there often, but I have been there once. it's a very big country and the sector that the British are in is one that's been more peaceful and the Prime Minister pointed out as they should they're turning more and more of the day-to-day security over to the Iraqis as they get trained and they get plussed up in their own security forces so I think it's appropriate that the British downsize their force. I don't think it has anything to do with the president's decision to increase u.s. forces in central Baghdad to back up the Iraqis who are doing the same thing going out more and more into the central capital to regain control of the of the capital city",
