    "turn_text": "Well, you're one of the few that's pointed out that it is non-binding. So what that means is it's all politics and all symbolism. It has no force of law. I think it's cynical on behalf of Nancy Pelosi to put a resolution like that up on the floor, I'd much rather have a real debate on a real vote that if it passes or fails that it has the force of law, it passes. So the resolution itself tried to have it both ways, and in addition to being non-binding part A, that we support our troops, and then part B, I said but we don't support the president's decision to reinforce those very same troops. So it's self-contradictory in two",
