    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91580.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 27,
    "turn_text": "Well, I can't speak for every, I do think Speaker Pelosi and the new Majority Leader, Senator Hoyer, the Democratic Majority, even immediately after 9-1-1 was not real excited about utilizing the military option of course the longer we've been in the field in the the more uh... uh... complicated the situation on the ground has become with all the various factions fighting for political power in iraq the blessed they supported the military option but having said that it is in our national security to fight world terrorism international you know islamic militant terrorism and uh... To do that, you have to be engaged militarily in Iraq and in Afghanistan. And because of that, I continue to support the President's decisions and continue to support a program that would lead towards victory. And I think we can win in Iraq.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_05",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "I continue to support the President's decisions regarding military engagement.",
