    "turn_idx": 65,
    "turn_text": "Okay, great. Thanks, James. Thanks for your call, and we do continue to take your calls here on Jerry Johnson Live. And I might mention that there's an event coming up that you need to be aware of, and that is something we call here at the Criswell College. encounter Chryswell and it takes place next Wednesday from 8 to 12 a.m. That's March 1st, 8 to 12 encounter Chryswell and what you can do is check out the Chryswell College. You can go to class, you can worship in the chapel, you can have lunch with professors and basically you can encounter the Chryswell College. To find out more about this you can give us a call at 800-899-0012 or you can go to the website www.criswell.edu or you can email us at mission at chriswell.edu. We hope that you will join us also. This is an announcement that I've been waiting to make. We now have archived shows. We have archived editions of Jerry Johnson Live on our website, which is at www.jerryjohnsonlive.com. And you can go back and hear shows that you've missed. We've been getting a lot of requests for the shows and we've been sending out CDs. But that is a little bit bulkier and a little bit more difficult. We're going to streamline the process now. And you can just go to the website www.jerryjohnsonlive.com and you can get the archived shows. As Kirby Anderson discussed yesterday, there's still a lot of opposition to Governor Rick Perry's mandate for the vaccine against the human papillom of virus, a sexually transmitted disease, basically, for 11 and 12-year-olds. We're going to talk with a doctor about the health implications of this, pro and con, so we hope that you will stay with us for more of Jerry Johnson Live. I'm Penny Dexter.",
