    "turn_idx": 87,
    "turn_text": "It seems like we're assuming that almost everybody's going to get this virus. And indeed, the data shows that most women by the age of 50 have HPV. However, those statistics, I haven't looked at those closely, the work virus. So you get the little words on your fingers is also an HPV. So I don't know if they're just saying that you can get some of the ones that aren't sexually transmitted. I don't know how they get that data. We do know that the work virus that causes the cancer has to be from sexual contact and that even if you have the wart on the skin, you're not going to get cervical cancer from that. It has to be in the genital tract",
