    "turn_text": "Well the bottom line is it just hasn't been tested sufficiently in males yet that's still on the horizon and they don't get cervical cancer they can get cancer of the penis and other parts of the genital tract they can get other cancers and other parts of the body but The incidence of those cancers is a lot lower than cervical cancer. So mainly the one thing about Gardasil that I think might sell for the guys is that it does also protect or at least provide some protection as far as we can tell against some of the warts and that's the thing that's going to bother them the most.",
