  {
    "episode_id": 91580,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91580.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 106,
    "turn_text": "The risks are out there and she's got cervical cancer. She engaged in, I'm not sure whether it was premarital, extramarital or marital sex, but she did receive the human papilloma virus and she got cervical cancer and she's dying. The risks are out there, but do those risks merit our mandating a sex virus vaccine to 11 and 12 year olds. That's the question that the Texas legislature is dealing with right now and grappling with as they repudiate or attempt to repudiate this executive order by Governor Rick Perry saying that all girls entering middle school should get the vaccine against this virus, really a sexually transmitted disease. So that's what we're discussing along with the idea of civil unions, really benefits of marriage for gay couples taking place in New Jersey. Is that or is that not a good idea? And of course, Tony Blair's announcement that Great Britain will pull troops out of Iraq beginning this summer and they're going to do this on a gradual basis. The number 800-8819270, we do have lots of calls. Let's go now to Gail in Fort Worth. Hi, Gail, thanks for calling.",
