        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker believes vaccines for sexually transmitted diseases should not be mandated for minors.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "Sexual activity among minors is a relevant consideration in medical policy decisions.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "The state’s role in enforcing vaccination is inherently coercive and ethically problematic.",
        "confidence": 0.86
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Assert / Elaborate"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 91580,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91580.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 110,
    "turn_text": "You know, a lot of times vaccines are mandated because it's a public health issue and they want to protect the general public health. A lot of people disagree with any vaccines and then they have to opt out on a philosophical basis. But in this case, it's a different ballgame. I agree with you, Gail, that this is a behavioral disease. And there's just no two ways around that. And so you either combat it with trying to change behavior among that risk group or you come and giving them the opportunity to get the vaccine if science develops a vaccine, but you don't mandate it.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
