  {
    "episode_id": 91580,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91580.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 119,
    "turn_text": "All right. I think the guests that you had just a few minutes ago gave very important, very succinct, and very detailed information, and that's probably one of the best information I've heard on any program in the news. And there was one comment that I think it was very quick, and a lot of people may not have paid attention to the comment, but she said, that this vaccine does protect only 70% of the patients or the individuals that get this cervical cancer, only 70% is caused by this virus. In other words, having the vaccination does not assure you that you won't get cervical cancer in the future.",
