        "text": "The speaker considers themselves qualified to judge the quality of information presented on news programs.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "The audience has access to the same information as the speaker and should recognize its importance.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "A high degree of detail and clarity is necessary for information to be considered valuable.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker believes that missing subtle points in a discussion undermines understanding of health risks.",
        "confidence": 0.86
      },
      {
        "text": "Vaccination provides protection only if the disease is fully preventable by the vaccine.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Assert / Elaborate"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 91580,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91580.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 120,
