    "turn_idx": 132,
    "turn_text": "It's a slippery slope and they're working on developing an AIDS vaccine and you know what concerns me is when you give a vaccine you actually give a little bit of that virus and in some people it does create a reaction and we haven't seen this going out in the larger population yet and we really don't know what the repercussions It's an experiment on 11-year-olds and it's not a good idea. Well, we've been talking today about really a couple of instances of the government facilitating sin through legislation. When you mandate a vaccine that really inoculates against some sexual misbehavior, you're facilitating sin. When you pass along the state of New Jersey or another state, that brings civil unions, the benefits of marriage for those who practice homosexual behavior, really anal sex, you are facilitating sin. And when I was at the National Religious Broadcasters Convention, I heard Senator John McCain, he actually visited us there along with Mitt Romney and Sam Brownback, And John McCain said that he could not support same-sex marriage, but he couldn't also pass a federal amendment against it, and that he really thinks the state should decide about these civil unions, about these benefits of marriage. So I think that's an important thing to keep in mind, as you consider these candidates for election. Well, 1 Corinthians 6 says, flee sexual immorality. That means premarital immorality. That means extramarital immorality. It also means homosexual behavior. The government is not to encourage it, and when states like Texas have wonderful abstinence curriculums, the government is not to undermine it and not to undermine parents who are trying to raise their children in the wisdom and the knowledge of the Lord. That's my thought on this issue, and we'll have more tomorrow on Jerry Johnson Live.",
